        "intent/0001/reviews/domain/remediation/SIGNED-LOG-SPEC.candidate.md:105-119"
      ],
      "impact": "The negative table says every other byte is unchanged. Changing decision in the stored/base event while retaining the supplied positive baseBytes causes validation step five to emit CANONICALIZATION_MISMATCH before step six can emit the declared EVENT_DIGEST_MISMATCH. If baseBytes is silently regenerated, the declared code is reached, so two conforming readings differ.",
      "requiredResolution": "State the complete mutated vector bytes or explicitly say that SLV1-NEG-001 regenerates supplied baseBytes from the mutated base event while retaining only eventDigest and signature. Alternatively change its expected code to CANONICALIZATION_MISMATCH. Then independently reproduce all nine vectors and refresh every affected digest and binding."
    },
    {
      "id": "R4-002",
      "severity": "major",
      "affects": ["PF-003", "R2-002", "SEC-G2-004"],
      "summary": "Permissions v2 defines an allowlist for supplied selectors but not a required-selector predicate, so omitted authorization context can pass.",
      "evidence": [
        "intent/0001/reviews/domain/remediation/PERMISSIONS-MANIFEST.candidate.json#grammar.comparison",
        "intent/0001/reviews/domain/remediation/PERMISSIONS-MANIFEST.candidate.json#principals.verified-human-session.applicationAuthorizations",
        "intent/0001/reviews/domain/remediation/PERMISSIONS-MANIFEST.candidate.json#principals.github-app-installation"
      ],
      "impact": "Because the rule checks only supplied selectors, a caller can omit organization, active-hat, repository, ref, assignment, execution, or authorization-state selectors and still meet the written comparison. Provider/application separation is also incomplete for GitHub pull_requests:write, which has no named application action mapping.",
      "requiredResolution": "Define selector-set semantics that require every selectorsExact value for the selected action, reject missing, duplicate, or unknown selectors, and define prefix fields as additional required or optional constraints explicitly. Map every write-capable provider permission to at least one exact application action and fail any unmapped permission. Refresh all affected digests and bindings."
    }
  ],
